{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "e0d9a1c2-4f3b-4a71-9c55-9b1f2a7c0011",
    "name": "EduGate PSP API v1",
    "description": "Server-to-server API for Payment Service Providers.\n\n**Amounts are integer tiyin.** 1 UZS = 100 tiyin, so 120000000 tiyin = 1 200 000.00 UZS. Never send a decimal.\n\n**Envelope.** Success is `{\"status\":\"ok\",\"data\":…}`; a handled error is `{\"status\":\"error\",\"error\":{\"code\",\"message\"}}`. Two cases still fall back to Laravel's default shape — see the \"Error cases\" folder.\n\n**Run order.** `Auth → Login` first: its test script stores the bearer token, and every other request inherits it. Then `Payments → Check` (stores `check_id`) before `Confirm`.\n\n**Confirm moves money.** It debits the PSP deposit and writes append-only rows that cannot be deleted. Point `base_url` at a local or sandbox cabinet unless you intend a real transaction.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
