    {
      "name": "3 · Payments",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Check — student + amount owed",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"institution_id\": {{institution_id}},\n  \"student_id_number\": \"{{student_id_number}}\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/payments/check",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "payments",
                "check"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Step 1. Resolves the student and what they owe, and issues a `check_id` valid for **15 minutes**.\n\nOmit `amount` (as here) and you get the full outstanding balance. Send `\"amount\": 50000000` to quote a part payment instead.\n\nMoves no money. The check lives in cache, not the database."
          },
          "response": [],
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "// Write to the active environment when there is one — an environment value",
                  "// otherwise shadows the collection variable and the request sends a stale blank.",
                  "const put = (k, v) => (pm.environment.name ? pm.environment : pm.collectionVariables).set(k, v);",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const d = pm.response.json().data;",
                  "pm.test('issues a check_id', () => pm.expect(d.check_id).to.match(/^chk_/));",
                  "pm.test('amount is integer tiyin', () => {",
                  "    pm.expect(d.amount_owed).to.be.a('number');",
                  "    pm.expect(d.amount_owed % 1, 'must not be fractional').to.eql(0);",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test('currency is UZS', () => pm.expect(d.currency).to.eql('UZS'));",
                  "put('check_id', d.check_id);",
                  "console.log('Owed:', (d.amount_owed / 100).toLocaleString(), 'UZS by', d.student.name);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Confirm — finalize (MOVES MONEY)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "Idempotency-Key",
                "value": "{{idempotency_key}}"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"check_id\": \"{{check_id}}\",\n  \"partner_transaction_id\": \"{{partner_transaction_id}}\",\n  \"amount\": 120000000,\n  \"gateway\": \"click\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/payments/confirm",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "payments",
                "confirm"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Step 2. Debits the PSP deposit, records commission, and applies the payment to the student's oldest unpaid schedules — all in one database transaction.\n\n`Idempotency-Key` is **required** (428 without it).\n\nDeduplication is on `(psp_id, partner_transaction_id)`, not on the header: replaying the same `partner_transaction_id` returns the original transaction untouched, even with a different key or amount. That is what makes a retry after a network timeout safe.\n\nThe pre-request script mints a fresh pair of ids on every run so this request always creates a new payment. The next request replays them deliberately.\n\n**amount is in tiyin** — 120000000 = 1 200 000.00 UZS."
          },
          "response": [],
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "prerequest",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "// Write to the active environment when there is one — an environment value",
                  "// otherwise shadows the collection variable and the request sends a stale blank.",
                  "const put = (k, v) => (pm.environment.name ? pm.environment : pm.collectionVariables).set(k, v);",
                  "",
                  "// Fresh ids per run, so this request always creates a NEW payment.",
                  "const stamp = Date.now();",
                  "put('partner_transaction_id', 'PT-' + stamp);",
                  "put('idempotency_key', 'idem-' + stamp);"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "// Write to the active environment when there is one — an environment value",
                  "// otherwise shadows the collection variable and the request sends a stale blank.",
                  "const put = (k, v) => (pm.environment.name ? pm.environment : pm.collectionVariables).set(k, v);",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('201 Created', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
                  "const d = pm.response.json().data;",
                  "pm.test('completed', () => pm.expect(d.status).to.eql('completed'));",
                  "pm.test('net = amount - commission', () =>",
                  "    pm.expect(d.net_amount).to.eql(d.amount - d.commission_amount));",
                  "pm.test('all amounts are whole tiyin', () =>",
                  "    ['amount', 'commission_amount', 'net_amount'].forEach(k =>",
                  "        pm.expect(d[k] % 1, k + ' must not be fractional').to.eql(0)));",
                  "put('transaction_id', String(d.id));",
                  "console.log('Txn', d.id, '· paid', (d.amount / 100).toLocaleString(),",
                  "            'UZS · commission', (d.commission_amount / 100).toLocaleString());"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Confirm — idempotent replay (no double charge)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "Idempotency-Key",
                "value": "a-completely-different-key"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"check_id\": \"{{check_id}}\",\n  \"partner_transaction_id\": \"{{partner_transaction_id}}\",\n  \"amount\": 999999999,\n  \"gateway\": \"click\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/payments/confirm",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "payments",
                "confirm"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Reuses the previous `partner_transaction_id` with a different Idempotency-Key AND a different amount.\n\nExpected: the ORIGINAL transaction comes back unchanged — same id, same amount. Nothing is charged twice. Run this straight after Confirm."
          },
          "response": [],
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const d = pm.response.json().data;",
                  "pm.test('returns the ORIGINAL transaction', () =>",
                  "    pm.expect(String(d.id)).to.eql(pm.variables.get('transaction_id')));",
                  "pm.test('amount was NOT overwritten by the replay', () =>",
                  "    pm.expect(d.amount).to.not.eql(999999999));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Get payment status",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/payments/{{transaction_id}}",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "payments",
                "{{transaction_id}}"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Scoped to the calling PSP — another PSP's transaction id returns 404, not 403, so ids cannot be probed."
          },
          "response": [],
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('is the transaction we created', () =>",
                  "    pm.expect(String(pm.response.json().data.id)).to.eql(pm.variables.get('transaction_id')));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
